From 707e4a60d0c4851123f1d3de921a57e89a2a7427 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:45:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] r36 AI selector: Classic (default) / Enhanced
 (experimental), fixed per duel

Kevy 4 Nov 11:09: experimental Enhanced preview, old AI kept as Classic. ChatGPT RELAY-105 readiness:
- one exact recipe (ai/midgame-flags.mjs AI_MODES): Classic = every r36 switch off; Enhanced = A+B; C/T/Z off
- cold load = Classic (select default, nothing stored); a change applies to the next new duel (worker.mjs
  sets the mode at 'start'; imported replays run Classic); every think names its mode and ai-worker.mjs sets
  it per think (no stale global); stale thinks are already discarded by id/revision
- Finding B (Enhanced only): worker.mjs passes its local pilot's pendingRemoval in the think message and
  ai-worker.mjs puts it on the fresh pilot, so B1's follow-up reaches the played move in the browser
- match banner names the AI mode
Tests: tests/r36-ai-mode.test.mjs (10, real ai-worker in Node; each changed file minus the selector lines =
r35.12 bytes). Tools: r36-ai-mode-browser.mjs (Playwright, 3 devices), r36-classic-parity.mjs.
Base: r36 F1 (73e2d07) + r35.12 (cc84a5f, d3177e0 cherry-picked). Builder: Claude; SELF-VERIFIED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HYdavRJmQWYnZCPQsymeGW
